# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `unreachable_statement`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: a statement after a `return` is dead code, never run.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w10-unreachable_statement), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

function f() -> i64
    return 1
    print(9)  #~ unreachable_statement

function main()
    print(f())
